From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terezi <jules@foxtails.me>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep unsupported beacon watch offline on 3DS

The main menu starts passive DS wireless discovery even in offline play.
The wireless stubs reject the scan and reset, leaving its shutdown waiting
and the communication state and status icon alive. Trainer Card then sees
a connected state and disables signing.

Skip this unsupported watcher on 3DS, report no discovered games, and make
its stop operation inert. Main menu saved Mystery Gift flags remain handled
by the menu itself. Other communication entry points keep their behavior.

---
diff --git a/src/comm_state.c b/src/comm_state.c
--- a/src/comm_state.c
+++ b/src/comm_state.c
@@ -957,22 +957,33 @@
 }
 
 void CommState_StartBeaconWatch(SaveData *saveData) {
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    // DS wireless beacon scanning is unavailable on the 3DS port.
+    (void)saveData;
+#else
     if (!Comm_IsActive()) {
         Heap_CreateAtEnd(HEAP_ID_3, HEAP_ID_15, 0x7000);
         CommState_Init(saveData, 17);
         sCommState->beaconId = 0;
         CommState_SetState(CommState_BeaconWatchInit, 0);
     }
+#endif
 }
 
 void CommState_StopBeaconWatch(void) {
+#ifndef SDK_PORT_3DS
     if (sCommState) {
         CommState_SetState(CommState_ShutdownWaitStopped, 5);
     }
+#endif
 }
 
 u8 CommState_GetSeenGames(void) {
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    return 0;
+#else
     return sCommState->seenGames;
+#endif
 }
 
 BOOL CommState_StopForReset(void) {
